{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the inadequate floorspace for Flat B at first floor resulting in the loss of a policy complaint 2 bed 3 person unit and the insufficient floorspace and head height for Flat C at loft level, would result in a sub-standard form of accommodation that would not be able to cater for the reasonable needs of future occupiers, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan 2021, Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010, Policy DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Nationally Described Space Standard (2015) as well as the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed rear dormer in combination with outrigger extension by virtue of their design, scale, siting, dimensions and awkward relationship with the existing two storey rear outrigger would give rise to a contrived and bulky form of development that would be detrimental to the visual amenities of Devonshire Road, Devonshire Close and Green Lane (partially).  Additionally, the dormer and outrigger extension would create additional bulk to the roofscape to represent a dominant and incongruous addition and awkward relationship with the parent roof slope, thereby both unbalancing and detracting from the character and symmetry of the prevailing build form within the street scene. The proposal would therefore fail to preserve the character and appearance of the application dwelling and the wider setting, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Core Strategy, DMD8, DMD13 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document as well as the aims and intentions outlined within the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed outrigger extension by reason of its design, scale and siting would constitute an obtrusive and overly dominant form of development, resulting in an unacceptable loss of light, outlook, and an increased sense of enclosure detrimental to the occupiers of the adjoining neighbouring property at No. 95 Devonshire Road. In this respect, the proposal would be contrary to policy CP30 of the Core Strategy and policies DMD8 and DMD13 of the Development Management Document."
  ],
